 The checks exercise actual file watchers and a Loader Include: malformed user YAML during bundle installation, recovery, additive manifest discovery, new bundle configuration watches, explicit disable/enable, retention on removal or version change, no commit during prepare, quiescent in-flight refresh disposal, and disposal while registration opens. The final case gates watcher readiness around the real registration to make the race reproducible; it does not substitute a fake watcher.
 
 Not established: code HMR, byte-level integrity of transitive dependencies, active AutoReview cancellation safety, runtime CLI package-manager races, and browser graph arrival. These require separate acceptance before deployment.
+
+## ISSUE-027 bounded real CLI acceptance (2026-09-03)
+
+`live-bundles-cli.smoke.mjs` runs the locally compiled changed CLI and app-boot, with immutable installed rc2 peers linked into an ancestor of a fresh private profile. It starts the actual web profile on localhost port 0, checks HTTP 200, then calls the same CLI's `plugin --profile web add fixture.tgz --offline --ignore-scripts --store-dir <private-store>`. Real pnpm 11.7.0 installs the zero-dependency local package and the CLI reconciles its manifest while web remains running. The test waits for activation, then runs ten consecutive disable/enable cycles with no inserted sleep. No model API, production profile, or external listener is used.
+
+Server-only small build configuration: `tsconfig.live-cli.json`; compile with the available TypeScript `tsc -p tsconfig.live-cli.json --pretty false`. This is a strict, noEmitOnError build of the reachable CLI/app-boot slice, not a monorepo typecheck. Build artifacts require the CLI package.json and config alongside the compiled files, plus read-only installed rc2 peer node_modules links. The configuration records this test server's type roots explicitly, and is not a general installation recipe.
+
+Run with `DSH_LIVE_EVIDENCE_PARENT=/srv/pi-lab-dev/tmp/dsh-live-bundle-cli-acceptance node --test apps/cli/tests/live-bundles-cli.smoke.mjs` after building. The immutable successful no-sleep evidence is `cli-live-uLERva` under that parent: web stdout, real pnpm output, final profile manifest, result.json and exit.json. Earlier `cli-live-48sZJF` retains the pre-fix failure: install and disable succeeded but the immediate enable was lost. `cli-live-nLNrfB` and `cli-live-XZPMSJ` used an artificial 200ms interval and are NOT no-sleep regression proof.
+
+Root cause: pinned installed chokidar 4.0.3 index.js lines 506-508 suppresses same-path change events within 50ms. `_throttle` lines 550-575 increments a count without extending the timer or emitting a trailing event. The composed watcher therefore waits 60ms before reading the latest configuration, then rechecks disposal. The ordinary single-file branch is unchanged. This is a dependency-specific bounded settle, not general arbitrary watcher-loss recovery. The smoke suite additionally verifies disposal during this delay never applies the queued file change (4/4 tests).
+
+Still not established: browser module arrival, live upgrade/removal of imported code, full upstream CI, and active AutoReview action cancellation. A tiny bundle installation does not prove arbitrary third-party package-install safety; lifecycle scripts are disabled here.
